  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html",
  "prefLabel": "En 1008.07 Reference Point of Applicability Review",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1008.07 Reference Point of Applicability Review. This process shall occur concurrently with fast track screening pursuant to En 1008.04:\n\n(a) If it is determined that the RPA is appropriate, the utility shall notify the applicant when it provides the screen results and proceed according to En 1008.04; and\n\n(b) If the utility determines that the RPA is inappropriate, the following shall occur:\n\n(1) The utility shall notify the applicant and with the notification include an explanation as to why it requires correction;\n\n(2) Upon receipt of notification from the utility the applicant shall provide the utility with a corrected application with the proper RPA within 5 business days of notification;\n\n(3) The utility shall review the corrected application with the proper RPA within 5 business days of receipt;\n\n(4) If the proper RPA is provided, the utility will proceed according to En 1008.04; and\n\n(5) If the applicant does not provide the appropriate location or request an extension of time within the deadline, the application shall be deemed withdrawn.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
}
